ght:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Travel like a toddler </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/UwCldxGezGk-LdRnQ53ET4WzllE=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/10/29/1793304363888.png' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/UwCldxGezGk-LdRnQ53ET4WzllE=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/10/29/1793304363888.png\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">The writer and her son admire \"David\" by Gian Lorenzo Bernini at the Borghese Gallery. Photo: Carly Mallenbaum/Axios</div><p><em>Carly writes:</em></p><p><strong>Because we </strong><em>weren't going to change who we were once we had kids, </em>my travel-loving husband and I insisted on bringing our toddler on a very adult trip to Portugal and Italy this summer.</p><ul><li><strong>Think: museum visits, </strong>Airbnbs, history tours and restaurant reservations.</li></ul><p><strong>Why it matters:</strong> Of course, traveling with a toddler changed the pace of the trip.</p><ul><li><strong>It also changed</strong> what I considered worth noticing.</li></ul><p>🏟️ <strong>Zoom in: </strong>We splurged on a private Colosseum tour in Rome, but I couldn't even tell you when the arena was constructed. I was too busy looking at holes in the ancient stones with my 2-year-old.</p><ul><li><strong>I have not a single fact </strong>to share from the Doge's Palace in Venice, which we left quickly because I sensed a tantrum percolating. I can, however, describe the choreography of how suitcases go from conveyor belt to truck to plane at the Venice airport.</li></ul><p><strong>Traveling with my toddler</strong> redirected my attention.</p><ul><li><strong>I'm usually </strong>the tourist reading every museum plaque, absorbing the history, taking notes and trying to fit in.</li><li><strong>This time, </strong>I followed my son's lead.</li></ul><p>🖼️ <strong>At the Borghese Gallery </strong>in Rome, my son learned that announcing \"Bernini! Bernini! Bernini!\" in a very quiet museum made even serious tourists giggle. And I didn't rush to quiet him.</p><ul><li><strong>In a piazza, </strong>we<strong> </strong>kicked a soccer ball with Italian kids, and I didn't even think to stop for a photo.</li><li><strong>At a bar in Lisbon,</strong> he sat transfixed by a <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cubmF0aW9uYWxnZW9ncmFwaGljLmNvbS90cmF2ZWwvYXJ0aWNsZS9ob3ctZmFkby1tdXNpYy1vZmZlcnMtd2luZG93P3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB4555931a\" target=\"_blank\">fado</a> performance, and I didn't immediately reach for a translation or to write in my journal.</li></ul><p><strong>✈️ The big picture: </strong>We aren't the only parents naive or ambitious enough to travel with a little one.</p><ul><li><strong>A </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly90cmlwYWR2aXNvci5tZWRpYXJvb20uY29tL3RyYXZlbC10aHJvdWdoLWxpZmU_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa8c7bd55\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>Tripadvisor survey</strong></a> from 2024 found that 81% of new parents planned on traveling with their child. According to the travel site's <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.\" target=\"_blank\">2026 trend report</a>, experience bookings containing children's tickets increased 19% year over year.</li></ul><p><strong>\"People don't want </strong>to just do water slides and water parks,\" says Melissa Zimmerman, my friend and the founder of <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYW5kLXdlcmUtb2ZmLmNvbS8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB0835ad4d\" target=\"_blank\">And We're Off</a> travel agency. \"They want to bring their kids along for the adventure.\"</p><ul><li><strong>Making that work, </strong>she says, often comes down to choosing the right home base, scheduling around naps and leaving room for downtime.</li></ul><p><strong>🚤 The bottom line:</strong> My son didn't become our kind of tourist. I became his.</p><ul><li><strong>When I picture</strong> Venice now, I don't first see St. Mark's Square or the Rialto Bridge. I think of my son beside the canal, cataloging the boats: police boat, trash boat, \"red one.\"</li></ul><p><em><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tLzIwMjYvMTAvMzAvdHJhdmVsLXdpdGgta2lkcy10b2RkbGVyLWV1cm9wZT91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBfc4c89b9\" target=\"_blank\">Share this story</a>.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtYjViZjg0MzctZDQ4MS00MWY2LTk3NTEtMzE3M2ZiOGEzN2FkLmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBff45f2d3\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.291771/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Travel like a toddler&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A1 big thing: Travel like a toddler%0Ahttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2Fnewsletters%2Faxios-finish-line-b5bf8437-d481-41f6-9751-3173fb8a37ad.html%3Fchunk%3D1%26utm_term%3Demshare%23story1\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-email-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Email this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/48174889.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-sms-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Text this Story\"></a></td></tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px 